<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovakia posts $847.2 mln Jan-July C/A deficit.</title>
<headline>Slovakia posts $847.2 mln Jan-July C/A deficit.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Slovak current account recorded a deficit for the January-July period in 1996 of $847.2 million, compared with a $488.5 surplus in the same period last year, the National Bank of Slovakia said on Friday.</p>
<p>The capital acccount was in surplus in the first seven months of the year by $949.9 million, compared with a surplus of $53.3 million in the same period last year.  </p>
<p>SLOVAK CURRENT ACCOUNT  Jan-Jul'96 Jan-Jun'96 Jan-Jul'95 FY/95</p>
<p>   overall ($million)	   -847.2     -737.1     +488.5   +648.8</p>
<p>   trade balance	  -1,048.0     -887.8	-13.7    +24.1</p>
<p>   balance of services    +102.1	+59.5     +434.9   +546.2</p>
<p>   income balance	    +25.3	+34.8	+39.4    -13.7</p>
<p>   current transfers	 +73.3	+56.4	+27.9    +92.2</p>
<p>SLOVAK CAPITAL ACCOUNT Total Capital and financial</p>
<p>   account balance	  +949.9	+707.9     +53.3   +993.9</p>
<p>   capital transfers	 +29.9	 +29.9     +45.7    +45.7</p>
<p>direct investment balance</p>
<p> inv. in Slovak republic   +98.1	 +63.9     +58.6   +141.9</p>
<p> Slovak investment abroad   -8.2	  -1.5	-5.1     -7.9</p>
<p>portfolio investment balance</p>
<p> inv. in Slovak Republic    +9.9	  +9.8	 n/a    +74.4</p>
<p> Slovak investment abroad  +49.9	 +30.7	 n/a   +171.7</p>
<p>other long-term financial</p>
<p>  account		     +352.1	+236.6     +77.8   +393.8</p>
<p> short-term fin. account  +418.1	+338.5    -137.8    +91.3</p>
<p>Note. All figures are in millions of U.S. dollars. Figures are subject to parliamentary approval. The central bank used the following exchange rates in calculating the figures: Jan-July '96 (USD=30.435 SKK), Jan-June'96 (USD=30.383 SKK), full year '95 (USD=29.735 SKK), Jan-July '95 (USD=29.746).</p>
<p>-- Peter Laca, Bratislava Newsroom, 42-7-536-3687</p>
